cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Nexium in your work, cite it as below."
title: "Nexium: a systems language that compiles to C, with ownership without a borrow checker and a checked effect system"
type: software
authors:
  - name: Londopy
    website: https://github.com/Londopy
version: 1.4.0
date-released: 2026-09-25
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/Londopy/nexium
url: https://londopy.github.io/nexium/
abstract: >-
  Nexium is a programming language whose compiler, written in Nexium and
  bootstrapped from one C file, emits C and drives a C compiler. The language
  has ownership with move semantics and reference counting instead of a
  garbage collector or a borrow checker, view rules that keep a reference
  from outliving its storage, a checked effect system that says whether a
  function allocates, blocks or can panic, binary patterns, compile-time
  evaluation, and one compiler that turns a source tree into a binary, a C
  library, a Python wheel, a Rust crate or an npm package.
keywords:
  - programming language
  - compiler
  - effect system
  - ownership
  - C
